From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:04:35 +0000
Subject: Fix channel logo check in unbranded builds

On Android, chrome://management builds its data source with
webui::CurrentChannelLogoResourceId(). Without Google Chrome branding, that
function calls CHECK_IS_TEST() for the canary, dev, beta and stable
channels. build/cromite.gn_args sets android_channel to "stable", so outside
tests the CHECK fails and opening chrome://management crashes the browser.
Return the generic product logo IDR_PRODUCT_LOGO_32 for these channels, the
same resource the unknown channel already uses.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
---
 chrome/browser/ui/webui/current_channel_logo.cc | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/current_channel_logo.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/current_channel_logo.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/current_channel_logo.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/current_channel_logo.cc
@@ -29,8 +29,7 @@ int CurrentChannelLogoResourceId() {
     case version_info::Channel::DEV:
     case version_info::Channel::BETA:
     case version_info::Channel::STABLE:
-      CHECK_IS_TEST();
-      [[fallthrough]];
+      return IDR_PRODUCT_LOGO_32;
 #endif
     case version_info::Channel::UNKNOWN:
       return IDR_PRODUCT_LOGO_32;
--
